jdk: https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/javase/jdk21-archive-downloads.html -> Windows x64 msi Installer	163.06 MB
sdk: https://jdk.java.net/javafx21/ -> Windows / x64	zip (sha256)	48050037 -> Store in jdk foler

🔹 1. Clone the Repo
After accepting invite:
in IntelliJ:
Open IntelliJ → Get from Version Control


Paste the repo URL and clone.



🔹 2. Install Same JDK and JavaFX SDK
To match your setup:
✅ JDK 21
 Download OpenJDK 21 from Oracle or Microsoft
 (You used jdk-21, so use the same exact version path)

https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/javase/jdk21-archive-downloads.html


✅ JavaFX SDK 21.0.2
 Download from: https://jdk.java.net/javafx21/



Then:
Extract JavaFX to: C:\Program Files\Java\javafx-sdk-21.0.2 (same as yours)


Set environment variable PATH_TO_FX (optional but helpful)



🔹 3. Open Project in IntelliJ
Open the cloned project folder


Let IntelliJ auto-import Maven (via pom.xml)


If JavaFX libraries don't link automatically:


Go to:
 File → Project Structure → Libraries → + → Java
 And add:

 vbnet
CopyEdit
C:\Program Files\Java\javafx-sdk-21.0.2\lib



🔹 4. Set Run Configuration
They should:
Go to Run → Edit Configurations


Add Application


Name: Main


Main class: org.example.Main


VM options:

 cpp
CopyEdit
--module-path "C:\Program Files\Java\javafx-sdk-21.0.2\lib" --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml



🔹 5. Build & Run
Just hit the green run button ▶️
 If everything is set right, the same JavaFX window will appear!

☑️ Final Tip
Tell them to commit and push using IntelliJ (Ctrl+K, then Ctrl+Shift+K) just like you.
Let me know if you want a shell script or .bat file to auto-setup all this.


